        "content": "<p><code>norm_num</code> disagrees with <code>#eval</code> and <code>ring_nf</code> on what the normal form of a rational number should look like:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">import</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Mathlib</span>\n\n<span class=\"sd\">/-- info: -3 / 2 -/</span>\n<span class=\"bp\">#</span><span class=\"n\">guard_msgs</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">in</span>\n<span class=\"bp\">#</span><span class=\"n\">eval</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"bp\">-</span><span class=\"mi\">3</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">/</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">2</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Rat</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">set_option</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">warn</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"gr\">sorry</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">false</span>\n\n<span class=\"sd\">/--</span>\n<span class=\"sd\">trace: foo : ℚ → Prop</span>\n<span class=\"sd\">⊢ foo (-3 / 2)</span>\n<span class=\"sd\">-/</span>\n<span class=\"bp\">#</span><span class=\"n\">guard_msgs</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">in</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">example</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">foo</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Rat</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Prop</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">foo</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"bp\">-</span><span class=\"mi\">3</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">/</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">2</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">ring_nf</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">trace_state</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"gr\">sorry</span>\n\n<span class=\"sd\">/--</span>\n<span class=\"sd\">trace: foo : ℚ → Prop</span>\n<span class=\"sd\">⊢ foo (-(3 / 2))</span>\n<span class=\"sd\">-/</span>\n<span class=\"bp\">#</span><span class=\"n\">guard_msgs</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">in</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">example</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">foo</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Rat</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Prop</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">foo</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"bp\">-</span><span class=\"mi\">3</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">/</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">2</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">norm_num</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">trace_state</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"gr\">sorry</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>I think we want these to agree. Should we change <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=Mathlib.Meta.NormNum.IsRat.neg_to_eq#doc\">docs#Mathlib.Meta.NormNum.IsRat.neg_to_eq</a> to match <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=Lean.instToExprRat#doc\">docs#Lean.instToExprRat</a> and <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=Mathlib.Tactic.RingNF.rat_rawCast_neg#doc\">docs#Mathlib.Tactic.RingNF.rat_rawCast_neg</a></p>",
        "id": 614821577,
